-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part II, Division A -- BENEFITS NOT PAYABLE (sections 44.1 and 44.2).
--
-- Section 44.1 takes the survivor's pension, the death benefit and the orphan's benefit away from an individual who has
-- been convicted of murdering (first or second degree) or manslaughtering the contributor, once the Minister is informed and
-- satisfied of it; it gives the benefit back if the conviction is reversed, and makes the individual repay what was paid.
-- Section 44.2 takes the survivor's pension away from a person who, after a division of earnings on a separation, did not
-- go back to the contributor in a new conjugal relationship for a year before the contributor died.
--
-- The Act leaves two things to others: the Minister's being "informed and satisfied" (a judgment, taken as a fact supplied
-- conditionally) and what is murder or manslaughter (the Criminal Code, which is not among the texts this piece reads). Both
-- are plain inputs. Every rule here is about what is done to the individual; there is no seat for the Minister.

§ `Part II -- Division A -- benefits not payable (sections 44.1 and 44.2)`

§§ `44.1(3), (6), (7) and (8) -- the conviction`

-- src:1042 | (i) has been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor,
-- src:1047 | Conviction outside Canada
-- src:1048 | (3) If an individual has been convicted by a court outside Canada in respect of an offence that, if it had been committed in Canada, would have constituted first or second degree murder or manslaughter, the Minister may deem that conviction to be a conviction of first or second degree murder or manslaughter for the purposes of this section.
-- src:1053 | Definition of first or second degree murder
-- src:1054 | (6) For the purpose of this section, first or second degree murder means murder within the meaning of section 231 of the Criminal Code.
-- src:1055 | Definition of manslaughter
-- src:1056 | (7) For the purpose of this section, manslaughter means manslaughter within the meaning of the Criminal Code.
-- src:1057 | Exception — probation order
-- src:1058 | (8) This section does not apply to an individual who is convicted of manslaughter if the individual is released on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under paragraph 731(1)(a) of the Criminal Code.
@ref Act s 44.1(1)(a)(i), (3), (6), (7), (8) (src:1042), (src:1047-1058)
GIVEN `the individual has been convicted of first or second degree murder of the contributor, murder within the meaning of section 231 of the Criminal Code` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual has been convicted of manslaughter of the contributor, manslaughter within the meaning of the Criminal Code` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual has been convicted by a court outside Canada of an offence that, if it had been committed in Canada, would have constituted first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister deems the conviction outside Canada to be a conviction of first or second degree murder or manslaughter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual convicted of manslaughter is released on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under paragraph 731(1)(a) of the Criminal Code` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: what counts as a conviction for section 44.1: a conviction of murder or manslaughter of the contributor in the
-- Criminal Code's senses, or a conviction outside Canada of an offence that would have been one if committed in Canada, which
-- the Minister "may deem" to be one (subsection (3)); but not a manslaughter conviction where the individual is released on
-- the conditions of a probation order under paragraph 731(1)(a) of the Criminal Code (subsection (8)).
-- out of range: sections 231 and 731(1)(a) of the Criminal Code (another statute, not among the inputs): murder, manslaughter and the probation order are taken as facts.
`s 44.1 — a conviction that engages this section` `the individual has been convicted of first or second degree murder of the contributor, murder within the meaning of section 231 of the Criminal Code` `the individual has been convicted of manslaughter of the contributor, manslaughter within the meaning of the Criminal Code` `the individual has been convicted by a court outside Canada of an offence that, if it had been committed in Canada, would have constituted first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor` `the Minister deems the conviction outside Canada to be a conviction of first or second degree murder or manslaughter` `the individual convicted of manslaughter is released on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under paragraph 731(1)(a) of the Criminal Code` MEANS
        (   `the individual has been convicted of first or second degree murder of the contributor, murder within the meaning of section 231 of the Criminal Code`
         OR `the individual has been convicted of manslaughter of the contributor, manslaughter within the meaning of the Criminal Code`
         OR (    `the individual has been convicted by a court outside Canada of an offence that, if it had been committed in Canada, would have constituted first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor`
             AND `the Minister deems the conviction outside Canada to be a conviction of first or second degree murder or manslaughter`))
    AND (NOT (    `the individual has been convicted of manslaughter of the contributor, manslaughter within the meaning of the Criminal Code`
              AND (NOT `the individual has been convicted of first or second degree murder of the contributor, murder within the meaning of section 231 of the Criminal Code`)
              AND `the individual convicted of manslaughter is released on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under paragraph 731(1)(a) of the Criminal Code`))

§§ `44.1(2) -- the conviction reversed`

-- src:1046 | (2) If the Minister is informed and satisfied that an individual’s conviction for first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor has been reversed, the charges have been withdrawn or the proceedings were stayed and not recommenced within the required time period and that all rights of appeal have been exhausted, the individual’s entitlement to the pension or benefit to which they would otherwise have been entitled under this Act shall be reinstated and any amount recovered from the individual shall be repaid.
@ref Act s 44.1(2) (src:1046)
GIVEN `the Minister is informed and satisfied that the individual's conviction has been reversed, the charges have been withdrawn, or the proceedings were stayed and not recommenced within the required time period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is informed and satisfied that all rights of appeal have been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: when the Minister is informed and satisfied that the conviction was reversed, the charges withdrawn or the proceedings stayed
-- and not recommenced in time, and that every right of appeal is used up, the individual's entitlement to what they would otherwise
-- have had is reinstated, and what was recovered from them is repaid.
`s 44.1(2) — the individual's entitlement is reinstated and any amount recovered is repaid` `the Minister is informed and satisfied that the individual's conviction has been reversed, the charges have been withdrawn, or the proceedings were stayed and not recommenced within the required time period` `the Minister is informed and satisfied that all rights of appeal have been exhausted` MEANS
    `the Minister is informed and satisfied that the individual's conviction has been reversed, the charges have been withdrawn, or the proceedings were stayed and not recommenced within the required time period` AND `the Minister is informed and satisfied that all rights of appeal have been exhausted`

§§ `44.1(1) -- the three benefits`

-- src:1038 | 44.1 (1) Despite section 44, a survivor’s pension, death benefit or orphan’s benefit is not payable to an individual in the following circumstances:
-- src:1039 | (a) in the case of the survivor’s pension, the individual who otherwise would have been entitled to receive the survivor’s pension as a result of the death of the contributor is not so entitled if the Minister is informed and satisfied that the individual has been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor;
@ref Act s 44.1(1)(a) (src:1038-1039)
GIVEN `the Minister is informed and satisfied that the individual has been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conviction engages section 44.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual's entitlement has been reinstated under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: a survivor's pension is not payable to an individual who would otherwise have been entitled, if the Minister is informed and
-- satisfied that the individual has been convicted of murder (first or second degree) or manslaughter of the contributor, unless entitlement has been reinstated under subsection (2).
`s 44.1(1)(a) — a survivor's pension is not payable to an individual convicted of killing the contributor` `the Minister is informed and satisfied that the individual has been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor` `the conviction engages section 44.1` `the individual's entitlement has been reinstated under subsection (2)` MEANS
    `the Minister is informed and satisfied that the individual has been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor` AND `the conviction engages section 44.1` AND (NOT `the individual's entitlement has been reinstated under subsection (2)`)

-- src:1040 | (b) in the case of the death benefit, the individual who otherwise would have been entitled to receive the death benefit under section 71 as a result of the death of the contributor is not so entitled if the Minister is informed and satisfied that the individual has been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor; and
@ref Act s 44.1(1)(b) (src:1040)
GIVEN `the Minister is informed and satisfied that the individual has been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conviction engages section 44.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual's entitlement has been reinstated under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: a death benefit is not payable under section 71 to an individual who would otherwise have been entitled, on the same footing.
-- out of range: section 71 (piece cp5): the death benefit to which the individual would otherwise have been entitled is paid under section 71.
`s 44.1(1)(b) — a death benefit is not payable to an individual convicted of killing the contributor` `the Minister is informed and satisfied that the individual has been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor` `the conviction engages section 44.1` `the individual's entitlement has been reinstated under subsection (2)` MEANS
    `the Minister is informed and satisfied that the individual has been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor` AND `the conviction engages section 44.1` AND (NOT `the individual's entitlement has been reinstated under subsection (2)`)

-- src:1041 | (c) in the case of the orphan’s benefit, the individual who otherwise would have been entitled to receive the orphan’s benefit as a result of the death of the contributor is not so entitled if the Minister is informed and satisfied that the individual
-- src:1042 | (i) has been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor,
-- src:1043 | (ii) has received an adult sentence for that murder or manslaughter, and
-- src:1044 | (iii) is 18 years of age or older.
@ref Act s 44.1(1)(c) (src:1041-1044)
GIVEN `the Minister is informed and satisfied that the individual has been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conviction engages section 44.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is informed and satisfied that the individual has received an adult sentence for that murder or manslaughter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the date on which it is asked whether the orphan's benefit is payable` IS A DATE
      `the individual's entitlement has been reinstated under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: an orphan's benefit is not payable to an individual who would otherwise have been entitled only if the Minister is informed and satisfied of three things: the
-- conviction, an adult sentence for it, and that the individual is 18 or older (section 2(2)'s deemed date), unless entitlement has been reinstated under subsection (2).
`s 44.1(1)(c) — an orphan's benefit is not payable to an individual convicted of killing the contributor` `the Minister is informed and satisfied that the individual has been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor` `the conviction engages section 44.1` `the Minister is informed and satisfied that the individual has received an adult sentence for that murder or manslaughter` `the individual's date of birth` `the date on which it is asked whether the orphan's benefit is payable` `the individual's entitlement has been reinstated under subsection (2)` MEANS
        `the Minister is informed and satisfied that the individual has been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor`
    AND `the conviction engages section 44.1`
    AND `the Minister is informed and satisfied that the individual has received an adult sentence for that murder or manslaughter`
    AND `s 2(2) — the person is treated as having reached a specified age on a date for a provision` `any other provision` `the individual's date of birth` 18 `the date on which it is asked whether the orphan's benefit is payable`
    AND (NOT `the individual's entitlement has been reinstated under subsection (2)`)

§§ `44.1(4) and (5) -- recovery, and the conviction before the section came into force`

-- src:1050 | (4) An individual who has received a pension or benefit referred to in this section and in respect of whom the Minister is subsequently informed and satisfied that the individual has been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor shall be deemed not to have been entitled to receive such pension or benefit, which shall constitute a debt due to Her Majesty under section 66 and the Minister shall recover those amounts, including any amounts paid before the date of the individual’s conviction.
@ref Act s 44.1(4) (src:1050)
GIVEN `the individual has received a pension or benefit referred to in section 44.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a bar of subsection (1) applies to the individual on what the Minister is now informed and satisfied of` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amounts the individual received, including any paid before the date of the conviction` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: an individual who received a survivor's pension, death benefit or orphan's benefit and about whom the Minister is later informed and satisfied of the
-- conviction is deemed not to have been entitled to it, and what was received, including what was paid before the conviction, is a debt due to Her Majesty under section 66,
-- which the Minister shall recover. The bar of subsection (1) is read as the one that applies: for an orphan's benefit that includes the adult sentence and age conditions of paragraph
-- (1)(c) (NOTES.md, fork register). NOTHING means the subsection creates no debt.
-- out of range: section 66 (piece cp4): the debt is due under section 66; only the amount is decided here.
`s 44.1(4) — the amount received that is a debt due to Her Majesty` `the individual has received a pension or benefit referred to in section 44.1` `a bar of subsection (1) applies to the individual on what the Minister is now informed and satisfied of` `the amounts the individual received, including any paid before the date of the conviction` MEANS
    IF `the individual has received a pension or benefit referred to in section 44.1` AND `a bar of subsection (1) applies to the individual on what the Minister is now informed and satisfied of`
    THEN JUST (sum `the amounts the individual received, including any paid before the date of the conviction`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1052 | (5) For greater certainty, this section applies in respect of any first or second degree murder or manslaughter conviction of which the Minister is informed before, on or after the coming into force of this section.
@ref Act s 44.1(5) (src:1052)
GIVEN time IS A `cp3 When the Minister is informed of a conviction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: the section applies to a conviction whether the Minister is informed of it before, on or after the section came into force: no
-- time of being informed takes a conviction out of the section. The text gives no date for the coming into force.
`s 44.1(5) — this section applies to a conviction of which the Minister is informed at a given time` time MEANS
    CONSIDER time
    WHEN `before the coming into force of section 44.1` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `on the coming into force of section 44.1` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `after the coming into force of section 44.1` THEN TRUE

§ `Part II -- Division A -- the survivor's pension after a division (section 44.2)`

-- src:1060 | 44.2 Despite paragraph 44(1)(d), a survivor’s pension is not payable to an individual as a result of a contributor’s death if, on or after January 1, 2025, a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings has taken place under paragraph 55.1(1)(b) between the contributor and that individual unless, at the time of the contributor’s death, that individual had been cohabiting with the contributor in a new conjugal relationship for a continuous period of at least one year.
@ref Act s 44.2 (src:1060)
`s 44.2 — the first day of 2025, from which a division under paragraph 55.1(1)(b) bars a survivor's pension` MEANS YearMonthDay 2025 1 1

-- src:1060 | 44.2 Despite paragraph 44(1)(d), a survivor’s pension is not payable to an individual as a result of a contributor’s death if, on or after January 1, 2025, a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings has taken place under paragraph 55.1(1)(b) between the contributor and that individual unless, at the time of the contributor’s death, that individual had been cohabiting with the contributor in a new conjugal relationship for a continuous period of at least one year.
@ref Act s 44.2 (src:1060)
GIVEN `a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings has taken place under paragraph 55.1(1)(b) between the contributor and the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which that division took place` IS A DATE
      `at the time of the contributor's death the individual had been cohabiting with the contributor in a new conjugal relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which that cohabitation began` IS A DATE
      `the day the contributor died` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: despite paragraph 44(1)(d), a survivor's pension is not payable to an individual as a result of a contributor's death if, on or after 1 January 2025, a division of
-- earnings took place between them under paragraph 55.1(1)(b), unless at the death the individual had been cohabiting with the contributor in a new conjugal relationship for a continuous
-- period of at least one year (counted as the core counts a year: the same calendar day a year later is a year).
`s 44.2 — a survivor's pension is not payable to an individual after a division of earnings` `a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings has taken place under paragraph 55.1(1)(b) between the contributor and the individual` `the day on which that division took place` `at the time of the contributor's death the individual had been cohabiting with the contributor in a new conjugal relationship` `the day on which that cohabitation began` `the day the contributor died` MEANS
        `a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings has taken place under paragraph 55.1(1)(b) between the contributor and the individual`
    AND `the day on which that division took place` AT LEAST `s 44.2 — the first day of 2025, from which a division under paragraph 55.1(1)(b) bars a survivor's pension`
    AND (NOT (    `at the time of the contributor's death the individual had been cohabiting with the contributor in a new conjugal relationship`
              AND `the day the contributor died` AT LEAST `the date a time limit ends` `the day on which that cohabitation began` (`a number of years` WITH `number of years` IS 1)))
